WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.157 --> 00:00:10.206
Consensus: how many targets at least 1, 2, 3 … of the tools predict.

2
00:00:10.206 --> 00:00:19.592
The UpSet plot shows which tools agree: each column is one combination of tools.

3
00:00:19.592 --> 00:00:26.250
Search by gene symbol, gene name or tool. HMGA2 is a well-known let-7 target.

4
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:35.377
Each row lists the tools that predict the target.

5
00:00:35.377 --> 00:00:42.010
Targets are sorted by how many tools predict them, so the best-supported come first.

6
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:46.847
Download every prediction as a zip.

7
00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:56.403
Enrichment tests the predicted genes against pathway and gene-set databases (human, mouse and rat).

8
00:00:56.403 --> 00:01:06.307
The organism follows the job's species. Keep the adjusted P-value cutoff at 0.05 and run.

9
00:01:06.307 --> 00:01:09.937
Enrichment runs in the background and usually takes about a minute.
